{"entryId":"3272","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3272:1","sourceSha256":"2a57d81655442fff90113b8fd81f59bf9d026327180a2908696f487b19065302","englishSha256":"da47ac8abbfcaa76f342b4a0d472af753ce5cd6b3e7796df3b8ecb0cb9bc7dee","citations":[{"id":"3272:1:link-001","he":[0,53],"en":[28,54],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_12b.1"},"reference":"Shabbat 12b:1","assessment":"The Bavli calls him a man of Jerusalem; Rashi calls him important and retains the spelling Shevna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 12b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_12b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 12b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3272:1:link-002","he":[0,53],"en":[56,61],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 12b:1:2","assessment":"The Bavli calls him a man of Jerusalem; Rashi calls him important and retains the spelling Shevna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 12b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Shabbat 12b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_12b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3272:1:link-003","he":[54,106],"en":[96,110],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 12b:1:2","assessment":"Tosafot in Shabbat attributes the one spelling to Rabbenu Tam, and gives Ri’s rationale for retaining Shevna, including his distinction between the two biblical figures.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 12b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3272:1:link-004","he":[108,134],"en":[251,262],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yoma_38b.4.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Yoma 38b:4:1","assessment":"Tosafot in Yoma reports the distinction and then argues that the two biblical Shevnas are one.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Yoma 38b:4:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yoma_38b.4.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3272:1:link-005","he":[135,163],"en":[294,315],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 12b:1:2","assessment":"Rabbenu Tam’s spelling with kaf is reported in the Shabbat Tosafot; Ri defends the spelling with bet.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 12b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,2,3,4],"holds":[{"raw":"ועי' תשובת מהרי\"ט בר\"פ שני דייני גזירות (ק\"ד) דשנים היו. וע\"ש בתוס'","reason":"The final responsum and folio reference require bibliographic collation. The checked Shabbat Tosafot preserves the distinction independently.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 12b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Tosafot in Shabbat contrasts Rabbenu Tam’s spelling and Ri’s defense of Shevna. Tosafot in Yoma gives a different identity judgment.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 12b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_12b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
